{"t":1789777200,"office":"LWX","station":"KDCA","point":"38.8894,-77.0352","field":"38.9429,-76.5684","field_station":"KNAK","afd":{"id":"499c56d2-752e-443e-ada7-51294e805011","office":"LWX","issuanceTime":"2026-09-18T18:52:00+00:00","productText":"\n000\nFXUS61 KLWX 181852\nAFDLWX\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Baltimore MD/Washington DC\n252 PM EDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\n.WHAT HAS CHANGED...\n\nAll sections were updated. \n\n&&\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n- 1) Cooler and drier conditions are forecast for Saturday, before\n     showers and thunderstorms return Sunday.\n\n- 2) Daily chances for showers persists into next week \n     along with cooler temperatures. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Cooler and drier conditions are forecast for Saturday, \nbefore showers and thunderstorms return Sunday.\n\nCdfnt will continue to push south of the area this afternoon\nwith isolated light showers ending from north to south, but\ncould linger through mid evening in central VA. Surface ridging\nbuilds in for Saturday supporting fair weather conditions. Warm\nair and moisture advection atop a shallow cool layer will\nsupport scattered showers across the northern half of the fcst\narea late Sat night into Sunday. Then, additional showers and\nthunderstorms are expected Sunday afternoon and evening along a\nretreating warm front. The front will sink south Sunday night as\nlow pressure passes by and high pressure starts building south\nagain. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Daily chances for showers persists into next week \nalong with cooler temperatures. \n\nUpper-level ridging breaks down early next week, with multiple \nshortwave disurbances moving across the Mid-Atlantic in the days \nfollowing. Mid-level moisture brought in from the south will \ncontinue overhead as winds flow northeasterly. As a result, daily \nshowers remain a possibility into late next week as these \ndisturbances slowly track across the region. Temperatures drop \non Tuesday in the wake of one of these disturbances, with highs \ngenerally ranging in the upper 50s and 60s. This cooler- than- \naverage weather persists at least through midweek as nearby \ndisturbances continue to bring rain showers to the area. Towards\nthe bay & coastlines, wind gusts could remain elevated mid-to- \nlate week as these disturbances begin to track offshore. \nOverall, coastal flooding could become something to watch out \nfor next week as these elevated winds combined with persistent \nrain stretches on. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION /18Z FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\n\nClouds expected to hang around tonight into Sat morning, but\ncigs should remain VFR. Clearing is expected Sat afternoon,\nbefore low clouds redevelop again toward Sunday morning. Low\nclouds/overcask skies will remain prevalent early next week. \n\nWinds generally flow north to northeasterly between Tuesday and \nWednesday. Showers and thunderstorms are possible each day, \npotentially bringing intermittent sub-VFR conditions across most \nterminals. Wind gusts gradually increase as the week continues.\n\n&&\n\n.MARINE...\n\nSCAs were issued for late tonight into Sat morning as winds\nstrengthen behind a northerly surge. Winds diminish Sat\nafternoon, but pick up again across the southern waters on\neasterly flow. \n\nWinds begin to increase starting Monday afternoon and could \npotentially approach gale conditions between Tuesday night and \nWednesday as a trough lingers near the waters. Showers & possibly a \nfew thunderstorms are possible during this period as the trough \nslowly moves out of the region. Depending on how slowly the trough \ntracks, winds could stay elevated into late next week. Winds \ngenerally flow northeasterly.\n\n&&\n\n.TIDES/COASTAL FLOODING...\n\nAs onshore flow strengthens next week, expect water levels to\nrise each day with minor coastal flooding becoming likely on\nMonday and possibly reaching moderate category by mid next week.\n\n\n&&\n\n.LWX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...\nDC...None.\nMD...None.\nVA...None.\nWV...None.\nMARINE...Small Craft Advisory from 10 PM this evening to 10 AM EDT \n     Saturday for ANZ531>533-539>541.\n     Small Craft Advisory from 5 AM to 1 PM EDT Saturday for ANZ534-\n     537-543.\n     Small Craft Advisory from 5 PM Saturday to 1 AM EDT Sunday for \n     ANZ534-537-543.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...LFR/KJP/SRT\nAVIATION...LFR/KJP/SRT\nMARINE...LFR/KJP/SRT\n"},"forecast":{"t":1789777179,"days":{"2026-09-18":{"hi":null,"lo":64,"pop":2,"short":"Mostly Cloudy"},"2026-09-19":{"hi":80,"lo":68,"pop":10,"short":"Partly Sunny"},"2026-09-20":{"hi":84,"lo":68,"pop":64,"short":"Mostly Cloudy then Chance Showers And Thunderstorms"},"2026-09-21":{"hi":77,"lo":64,"pop":54,"short":"Chance Rain Showers"},"2026-09-22":{"hi":68,"lo":59,"pop":59,"short":"Rain Showers Likely"},"2026-09-23":{"hi":64,"lo":58,"pop":50,"short":"Chance Rain Showers"},"2026-09-24":{"hi":66,"lo":57,"pop":45,"short":"Chance Showers And Thunderstorms"},"2026-09-25":{"hi":70,"lo":null,"pop":23,"short":"Slight Chance Rain Showers"}}},"grid":{"t0":1789776000,"n":48,"ceil":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,25000,25000,25000,25000,25000,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],"vis":[10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,5.0,5.0,5.0,4.0,4.0,4.0],"spd":[7,7,8,8,8,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,8,8,7,7,8,8,8,9,9,9,9,9,8,8,7,7,7,7,7,7,8,9,10,11,12,12,12,12,12,11,10,8],"gst":[8,8,9,9,9,10,10,10,10,10,10,10,10,10,10,10,9,9,8,8,9,9,9,10,10,10,10,10,9,9,8,8,8,8,8,8,9,10,14,15,17,17,17,17,17,15,14,9],"dir":[10,10,20,20,20,20,30,30,30,30,30,40,40,40,50,60,60,70,70,80,90,100,100,110,110,110,120,120,120,130,130,140,140,140,150,160,170,170,180,180,180,190,190,190,190,190,190,